### Shipzy Backend - Auth API Testing
### Use REST Client extension in VS Code or similar tools

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@apiUrl = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1

# Variables - Replace with your actual tokens
@firebaseIdToken = YOUR_FIREBASE_ID_TOKEN_HERE
@accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@refreshToken = YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. API Version
GET {{apiUrl}}

###
### ============ AUTHENTICATION ENDPOINTS ============
###

### 3. Firebase Verify - New User (Client)
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/firebase/verify
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: test-device-123

{
  "idToken": "{{firebaseIdToken}}",
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "role": "client"
}

### 4. Firebase Verify - New User (Courier)
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/firebase/verify
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: test-device-456

{
  "idToken": "{{firebaseIdToken}}",
  "fullName": "Jane Driver",
  "role": "courier"
}

### 5. Firebase Verify - Existing User (Login)
# Only idToken is required for existing users
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/firebase/verify
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: test-device-123

{
  "idToken": "{{firebaseIdToken}}"
}

### 6. Refresh Token
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 7. Logout
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
### ============ ERROR TESTING ============
###

### 8. Test Invalid Token
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token-here

### 9. Test Missing Required Field
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/firebase/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test User"
}

### 10. Test Rate Limiting
# Make multiple rapid requests to trigger rate limit
POST {{apiUrl}}/auth/firebase/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idToken": "test"
}

### 11. Test 404 Not Found
GET {{apiUrl}}/nonexistent-endpoint

###
### ============ CURL EXAMPLES (for terminal) ============
###

# Health Check
# curl http://localhost:3000/health

# Firebase Verify
# curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/firebase/verify \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -H "X-Device-Id: test-device-123" \
#   -d '{
#     "idToken": "YOUR_FIREBASE_TOKEN",
#     "fullName": "John Doe",
#     "role": "client"
#   }'

# Refresh Token
# curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/refresh \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{
#     "refreshToken": "YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN"
#   }'

# Logout
# curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/logout \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN"

